    "explanation": "To both parties: this case cannot be decided on the present record, so it goes to a human reviewer and the disputed SGD 8.60 is held — neither collected nor refunded — until that review is done.\n\nWhat both sides agree on, and I accept. There was no route deviation. EV-GPS-00719 measures 10.99 km against the booked optimal of 11.0 km on EV-TRIP-00719, an excess of −0.01 km (−0.09%). Both POL-RD-01 gates fail (not over 20% of optimal, not over 0.8 km), so no deviation is established however the trip is characterised, and the trace backing that measurement is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 (115 fixes, 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0.0 s). The trip is priced UPFRONT_QUOTE (EV-FARE-00719: quoted_fare_sgd 22.40, total_charged 22.40, charged_over_quote 0.00), so POL-RD-02 does not run and POL-RD-11 leaves no distance-or-time refund; and with no ERP, no airport surcharge and no waiting fee (properly_chargeable 0.00) POL-RD-09 gives no pass-through or billing-integrity correction. The 13.80 figure the rider relies on appears in no artifact — only in her own in-app message of 11:27:45 — so I treat it as her account of what the app showed, not a ledger fare.\n\nWhy the case nonetheless cannot be closed. The dropoff was amended: the pin moved roughly 80 m (from 'Original back-gate pin', 1.328/103.84678, to 'Central Gardens destination', 1.328/103.8475), and EV-TRIP-00719 carries dropoff_amended_at 2026-09-27T11:27:40. But amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are both null. POL-RD-05 requires the deviation test to be re-run against the route between the amended endpoints, and says in terms that where the amendment timestamp is present but that figure is missing, the re-quote is absent, the clause cannot be run, no substitute may be derived, and POL-RD-10(5) applies. POL-RD-10(5) names this exact state — 'a POL-RD-05 amendment with amended_optimal_distance_km null' — as a mandatory trigger. I therefore reject the driver's submission that POL-RD-05 is 'not reached' because the measured excess is negative: the clause is engaged by the amendment itself and its duty to re-baseline does not depend on there being a positive excess. The record is incomplete; that is a data failure, not a finding for either side. The driver's POL-RD-04 answer also fails — the pin move was requested by the driver ('Just move the pin to Block B, same price'), not the rider, and waypoint_hint is null on both messages, so the clause's corroboration test cannot be run. No traffic cause is asserted by either side, so the MISSING advisory (EV-ADVIS-00719-01, weight 0.0) escalates nothing by itself under POL-RD-13. And with driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 0 over 250 completed trips in 90 days, no POL-RD-06 pattern and no conduct referral arises.\n\nWhat would resolve it: the amended optimal distance and duration stored when the re-quote was issued (and, if available, the pre-move quoted fare). With those, the amended-baseline deviation test can be run and the rider's fare question answered. Confidence is 0.85; the deciding artifacts (EV-TRIP-00719, EV-GPS-00719, EV-FARE-00719, EV-CHAT-00719) all carry weight 1.0, so nothing in the ruling is discounted."
